# Graph behaviors receipt (plan 2026-08-13, slices W1b / W2 / W5): a pack
# declares WHEN it runs, the review names that before anything is granted, and
# a node appearing under the watched folder runs it with nobody asking.
# FRESH profile; requires the piccolo feature (the runnable lane).
settle 30
key escape

# The folder first, so the declared watch resolves to a real container and the
# member minted later has something to belong to.
#
# `file:///` rather than a web address: `containment_parent_url` covers
# http/https/file, and a real fetch can rewrite a node's URL out from under the
# watch that resolved to it. A receipt should not depend on the network.
#
# The trailing slash is load-bearing: the kernel names a containment parent in
# DIRECTORY form, so a watch on the slashless address contains nothing and is
# silently inert. That cost an afternoon to find; it is in the scenario so the
# next reader sees it stated.
open file:///notes/
settle 15

drop-file 200 200 scenarios/fixtures/inbox_filer.lua
settle 10
assert event denizen-staged
# The ruled install condition: when this runs, beside what it may touch,
# before either is granted. The row is a palette suggestion, which no assert
# verb reads, so this is a visual receipt; the text itself is asserted by
# `the_review_names_the_watch_and_confirming_registers_it`.
capture 01_review_names_the_watch

act Install inbox_filer
settle 15
assert event denizen-installed
# Folder, its content node, and the denizen's own node.
assert nodes >= 3
capture 02_installed

# Nothing invokes the behavior. A node simply appears under the folder.
open file:///notes/one
settle 20
assert event denizen-ran
# The discriminating count: the member the user opened is one node, and the
# one the behavior wrote is another. Had it not woken, this would be short by
# exactly one.
assert nodes >= 6
capture 03_woke_unasked

log behaviors_wake receipt complete
